   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Before and after",
     "texto": [
      "**Inden** (before) and **efter at** (after) introduce a subordinate clause: **Inden du går, skal du lukke døren.** = Before you leave, you have to close the door.",
      "**Efter at vi havde spist, gik vi en tur.** = After we had eaten, we went for a walk.",
      "With **efter at** the order is subordinate: subject before the verb."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "While, when and whenever",
     "texto": [
      "**Mens** (while) describes something happening at the same time. **Da** (when, once in the past) and **når** (when, always or in the future) show the moment.",
      "**Mens jeg laver mad, lytter jeg til radio.** = While I cook, I listen to the radio.",
      "**Da jeg var barn, boede vi i Aarhus.** = When I was a child, we lived in Aarhus.",
      "**Når jeg får fri, rejser jeg.** = When I have time off, I travel."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
